  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Mormon",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 4,
    "summary": "War and carnage continue—The wicked punish the wicked—Greater wickedness prevails than ever before in all Israel—Women and children are sacrificed to idols—The Lamanites begin to sweep the Nephites before them. About A.D. 363–75.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And now it came to pass that in the three hundred and sixty and third year the Nephites did go up with their armies to battle against the Lamanites, out of the land Desolation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 125,
            "text": "2 Ne. 1:12; Morm. 1:11 (11–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Mormon 4:1",
        "book": "Mormon",
        "chapter": 4,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the armies of the Nephites were driven back again to the land of Desolation. And while they were yet weary, a fresh army of the Lamanites did come upon them; and they had a sore battle, insomuch that the Lamanites did take possession of the city Desolation, and did slay many of the Nephites, and did take many prisoners.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 266,
            "end": 281,
            "text": "3 Ne. 3:23; Morm. 3:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "3 Ne. 3:23; Morm. 3:7.",
            "prettyString": "3 Nephi 3:23; Mormon 3:7",
            "references": [
              {
